*Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?*

N/A

*Operating system/version*

macOS 11.6 ( both M1 mac and Intel mac)

*Terminal name/version*

iTerm2/latest, kitty/latest, alatritty/latest

*$TERM environment variable*

xterm-256color

*Installation*

homeberw ( command: brew install neovim --HEAD)

*How to reproduce the issue*

• use neovim installed by homebrew (brew install neovim --HEAD)
• install plugins
    • <https://github.com/wbthomason/packer.nvim|packer>
    • nvim-treesitter
    • nightfox colorscheme (or other tree-sitter supported colorscheme like <https://github.com/rockerBOO/awesome-neovim#colorscheme|these>)
• use following minimal init.lua

```
vim.cmd [[packadd packer.nvim]]
require('packer').startup{
  function(use)
    use {'wbthomason/packer.nvim', opt = true}
    use {
      'nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter',
      config = function()
	require'nvim-treesitter.configs'.setup {
	  ensure_installed = "maintained",
	  highlight = {
	    enable = true
	  },
	  indent = {
	    enable = true,
	  },
	}
      end
    }
    use {
      'EdenEast/nightfox.nvim',
      config = function()
	vim.cmd [[colo nightfox]]
      end,
    }
  end,
}
```

• edit following python script

```
def test(*args):
    pass

a = 3;
b = 5;

test(3, 8)
test(1, b)
test(a, b)
```

